Scene 2: Describing a Person's Features

38
00:02:18,223 --> 00:02:22,122
Where is Mr. Tanaka?

39
00:02:22,146 --> 00:02:26,579
He’s in front of the station right now.

40
00:02:26,602 --> 00:02:31,602
There are a lot of people in front of the station, aren’t there?

41
00:02:31,625 --> 00:02:36,694
What is Mr. Tanaka wearing?

42
00:02:36,717 --> 00:02:40,287
He’s wearing a white jacket.

43
00:02:40,310 --> 00:02:43,912
What color are his pants?

44
00:02:43,936 --> 00:02:47,469
He’s wearing black pants.

45
00:02:47,492 --> 00:02:50,531
Is he wearing a hat?

46
00:02:50,555 --> 00:02:55,452
Yes, he’s wearing a brown hat.

47
00:02:55,475 --> 00:02:58,642
Is his hair long or short?

48
00:02:58,665 --> 00:03:00,701
Short?

49
00:03:00,725 --> 00:03:04,758
His hair is a little long.

50
00:03:04,781 --> 00:03:07,655
Is he carrying a bag?

51
00:03:07,679 --> 00:03:12,372
I have a big, yellow bag.

52
00:03:12,395 --> 00:03:16,329
That yellow bag really stands out!

53
00:03:16,352 --> 00:03:20,552
Is Mr. Tanaka tall?

54
00:03:20,575 --> 00:03:24,650
No, he's not very tall.

55
00:03:24,673 --> 00:03:28,330
Is he not wearing glasses?

56
00:03:28,354 --> 00:03:31,120
He isn't wearing glasses.

57
00:03:31,143 --> 00:03:35,777
There's a person over there wearing a brown hat.

58
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:39,875
Is that person wearing a white jacket?

59
00:03:39,898 --> 00:03:44,232
Yes, they're wearing a white jacket.

60
00:03:44,255 --> 00:03:47,539
Are they carrying a yellow bag?

61
00:03:47,562 --> 00:03:52,005
Oh, they have a small black bag.

62
00:03:52,028 --> 00:03:56,716
Well then, that person isn't Mr. Tanaka.

63
00:03:56,740 --> 00:04:01,012
What color are Mr. Tanaka's shoes?

64
00:04:01,036 --> 00:04:04,677
He's wearing red sneakers.

65
00:04:04,701 --> 00:04:09,472
Oh, there's someone over there in red sneakers.

66
00:04:09,495 --> 00:04:12,551
Is he wearing a hat?

67
00:04:12,575 --> 00:04:15,941
Yes, and a brown hat.

68
00:04:15,964 --> 00:04:18,580
Is the bag yellow?

69
00:04:18,604 --> 00:04:22,900
Yes, it's a big yellow bag.

70
00:04:22,923 --> 00:04:26,257
That must be Mr. Tanaka!

71
00:04:26,280 --> 00:04:35,359
Let me know if you caught all that in the comments!

72
00:04:35,359 --> 00:04:38,359
Scene 3: Introducing My Family Photos

73
00:04:38,359 --> 00:04:41,959
Is this a photo of your family?

74
00:04:41,982 --> 00:04:43,182
Yes,

75
00:04:43,205 --> 00:04:46,459
it's a photo we took last summer.

76
00:04:46,482 --> 00:04:51,732
Is this tall man your older brother?

77
00:04:51,756 --> 00:04:56,156
No, that's my younger brother.

78
00:04:56,179 --> 00:05:00,379
Your brother is really tall!

79
00:05:00,402 --> 00:05:02,002
Yes,

80
00:05:02,025 --> 00:05:05,203
He's 180 centimeters.

81
00:05:05,226 --> 00:05:09,959
He has short hair and looks like he's good at sports.

82
00:05:09,982 --> 00:05:11,198
Yes,

83
00:05:11,222 --> 00:05:14,280
He plays soccer every day.

84
00:05:14,304 --> 00:05:19,637
Is this beautiful woman your older sister?

85
00:05:19,660 --> 00:05:21,027
Yes,

86
00:05:21,050 --> 00:05:23,653
that's my sister.

87
00:05:23,676 --> 00:05:28,882
She has long hair, big eyes, and is really cute!

88
00:05:28,906 --> 00:05:32,202
My sister looks a lot like my mom.

89
00:05:32,226 --> 00:05:34,921
Which one is your mom?

90
00:05:34,945 --> 00:05:37,878
The person next to my sister.

91
00:05:37,901 --> 00:05:40,999
Does your mom have long hair too?

92
00:05:41,022 --> 00:05:45,224
No, my mom has short hair.

93
00:05:45,247 --> 00:05:47,664
She's wearing a kimono, isn't she?

94
00:05:47,688 --> 00:05:49,055
Yes,

95
00:05:49,078 --> 00:05:51,354
She wore it for New Year's.

96
00:05:51,377 --> 00:05:54,744
Where's your dad?

97
00:05:54,767 --> 00:05:58,700
The man with glasses in the back.

98
00:05:58,723 --> 00:06:03,090
Your dad has such a kind face.

99
00:06:03,113 --> 00:06:04,579
Yes,

100
00:06:04,602 --> 00:06:07,697
He's very serious and kind.

101
00:06:07,721 --> 00:06:10,688
Is your dad overweight?

102
00:06:10,711 --> 00:06:14,311
No, he's a little thin.

103
00:06:14,334 --> 00:06:18,367
You look like your dad!

104
00:06:18,390 --> 00:06:20,390
People tell me that all the time.

105
00:06:20,413 --> 00:06:24,213
Especially the shape of our noses—we look just alike!

106
00:06:24,236 --> 00:06:28,106
I see. That’s a little embarrassing.

107
00:06:28,130 --> 00:06:32,130
What a lively and fun-looking family!

108
00:06:32,153 --> 00:06:33,519
Yes,

109
00:06:33,542 --> 00:06:36,281
Everyone talks a lot.

110
00:06:36,305 --> 00:06:38,592
What a lovely photo!

111
00:06:38,615 --> 00:06:40,906
Thank you.

112
00:06:40,930 --> 00:06:43,930
Scene 4: Describing the Person at the Next Table

113
00:06:43,930 --> 00:06:47,930
Take a look at the person at the next table.

114
00:06:47,953 --> 00:06:49,807
Which one?

115
00:06:49,831 --> 00:06:54,317
The one reading a book alone over there.

116
00:06:54,341 --> 00:06:59,151
You mean the older man with short white hair?

117
00:06:59,174 --> 00:07:04,174
No, the young woman next to him.

118
00:07:04,197 --> 00:07:08,079
Ah, that beautiful woman.

119
00:07:08,103 --> 00:07:12,036
She has long, straight hair.

120
00:07:12,059 --> 00:07:16,126
I hear her eyes are a little blue.

121
00:07:16,150 --> 00:07:18,559
Is she a foreigner?

122
00:07:18,582 --> 00:07:22,116
Hmm, I’m not sure.

123
00:07:22,139 --> 00:07:25,105
She’s wearing a white dress.

124
00:07:25,128 --> 00:07:29,062
It suits her perfectly—so lovely.

125
00:07:29,085 --> 00:07:31,418
Is she tall?

126
00:07:31,441 --> 00:07:33,095
Short?

127
00:07:33,118 --> 00:07:38,094
She’s sitting, so I can’t tell, but she seems tall.

128
00:07:38,118 --> 00:07:41,485
Her hands are so slender and pretty.

129
00:07:41,509 --> 00:07:44,594
And her fingers are long.

130
00:07:44,617 --> 00:07:47,354
What’s she drinking?

131
00:07:47,377 --> 00:07:50,623
She’s having warm tea.

132
00:07:50,647 --> 00:07:53,516
What kind of bag does she have?

133
00:07:53,540 --> 00:07:58,173
There’s a black leather bag under the table.

134
00:07:58,196 --> 00:08:01,470
Is she wearing a watch?

135
00:08:01,493 --> 00:08:06,227
Yes, a small silver one.

136
00:08:06,250 --> 00:08:09,744
She’s reading so quietly.

137
00:08:09,767 --> 00:08:13,134
I wonder what kind of book it is.

138
00:08:13,157 --> 00:08:16,845
Looks like a book with difficult kanji.

139
00:08:16,868 --> 00:08:19,735
She seems really smart.

140
00:08:19,758 --> 00:08:23,524
Oh! She just checked her watch.

141
00:08:23,547 --> 00:08:26,992
Maybe she’s waiting for someone.

142
00:08:27,016 --> 00:08:30,291
Her smile is so cute.

143
00:08:30,315 --> 00:08:33,971
She’s really charming, isn’t she?

144
00:08:33,995 --> 00:08:36,995
Scene 5: Characteristics of Mr. Yamada

145
00:08:36,995 --> 00:08:41,974
Do you know the new employee, Mr. Yamada?

146
00:08:41,997 --> 00:08:44,531
I haven’t met him yet.

147
00:08:44,554 --> 00:08:46,487
What’s he like?

148
00:08:46,510 --> 00:08:51,477
He’s a very energetic and cheerful guy.

149
00:08:51,499 --> 00:08:54,366
Is she tall?

150
00:08:54,389 --> 00:08:58,522
No, he's not very tall.

151
00:08:58,545 --> 00:09:01,512
Is he big?

152
00:09:01,535 --> 00:09:06,668
He’s a little chubby, but he’s muscular.

153
00:09:06,691 --> 00:09:09,691
What’s his hairstyle like?

154
00:09:09,714 --> 00:09:14,563
He has short, black hair.

155
00:09:14,587 --> 00:09:17,638
Does he wear glasses?

156
00:09:17,661 --> 00:09:22,400
Yes, round glasses.

157
00:09:22,424 --> 00:09:25,958
Any distinctive facial features?

158
00:09:25,980 --> 00:09:29,870
His eyebrows are really thick.

159
00:09:29,894 --> 00:09:33,028
You have thick eyebrows, don’t you?

160
00:09:33,051 --> 00:09:35,852
That makes you easy to remember.

161
00:09:35,875 --> 00:09:40,494
And your ears are a little big too.

162
00:09:40,517 --> 00:09:43,331
What kind of voice do you have?

163
00:09:43,355 --> 00:09:48,688
It’s deep and really nice.

164
00:09:48,711 --> 00:09:52,346
What kind of suits do you usually wear?

165
00:09:52,370 --> 00:09:56,503
I often wear gray suits.

166
00:09:56,526 --> 00:09:59,462
What color is your tie?

167
00:09:59,485 --> 00:10:03,685
I’m wearing a red tie today.

168
00:10:03,708 --> 00:10:06,375
Are your shoes clean?

169
00:10:06,399 --> 00:10:11,244
Yes, my black leather shoes are always polished.

170
00:10:11,267 --> 00:10:14,201
You seem like a very meticulous person.

171
00:10:14,225 --> 00:10:19,258
Yes, you look like you work very efficiently.

172
00:10:19,281 --> 00:10:21,931
How old are you?

173
00:10:21,954 --> 00:10:25,188
I think he’s around 30.

174
00:10:25,211 --> 00:10:28,705
He seems young and reliable.

175
00:10:28,729 --> 00:10:32,895
Oh, that’s him making copies over there.

176
00:10:32,918 --> 00:10:36,328
The one with the round glasses, right?

177
00:10:36,352 --> 00:10:40,352
Yes, that’s Mr. Yamada.

178
00:10:40,375 --> 00:10:44,231
I’ll go say hello later.

179
00:10:44,254 --> 00:10:47,254
Scene 6: Identifying a Lost Child’s Features

180
00:10:47,254 --> 00:10:48,864
Excuse me.

181
00:10:48,887 --> 00:10:51,521
I’m looking for a lost child.

182
00:10:51,543 --> 00:10:54,013
What does the child look like?

183
00:10:54,037 --> 00:10:57,439
He’s a 5-year-old boy.

184
00:10:57,463 --> 00:11:00,111
What’s his name?

185
00:11:00,134 --> 00:11:02,409
His name is Takeshi.

186
00:11:02,433 --> 00:11:06,501
How tall is Takeshi?

187
00:11:06,524 --> 00:11:10,258
He’s about 100 centimeters tall.

188
00:11:10,281 --> 00:11:13,579
